WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:15.130
Since then nuclear deal, Iran has been debating
how much it should allow the rest of the world

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:20.930
in, how much investment is going to be permitted
for foreign companies to have in major concerns

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:23.500
like oil and manufacturing.

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.560
This has been a central debate between the
moderates and reformists, as well as the more

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.010
conservative hardliners.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:36.320
Moderates like President Rouhani want to allow,
say for example, 10, 15, 20% foreign investment

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.590
into a major Iranian concern.

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:42.990
Whereas those among the conservatives and
the more extreme hardliners really don't want

00:00:42.990 --> 00:00:44.600
any foreign investment at all.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:49.510
This of course has a huge historical precedence
because of the role that Britain and other

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:54.720
colonial powers played 100 years ago in controlling
Iran's oil industry.

00:00:54.720 --> 00:00:58.770
There's a lot of deep wounds still about that
issue, and I think this is going to be a real

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:04.049
challenge for the Iranian leadership to figure
out what way forward, how do we become rich

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:09.600
again and how much do we want to let the rest
of the world dictate terms of how we will

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:10.100
function economically.

